p("siman_039/turei-zahav/part-001.txt", "turei-zahav", {
  "1#_": `That she not eat meat — but something people are not particular about such as roasted grains and nuts — though affliction of soul and he can annul for her; nevertheless here with great particularity the matter depends; and this is specifically in great matters such as meat and wine and similar.`,
  "2#א": `Kiddushin voided — he thinks perhaps sage will not find opening to permit her — therefore certainly not agreeable to kiddushin.`,
  "2#ב": `Doubtfully betrothed — can say "I do not want a woman who vows"; also get not agreeable to give her since she is important daughter of great ones and my relatives forbidden to me — therefore not agreeable kiddushin take effect; and there are opinions who do not hold this reasoning — therefore needs get from doubt; why Tur wrote here needs get — meaning stringently; but non-important woman — all agree kiddushin certain whenever permitted before husband knew.`,
  "4#א": `Coarse from her peers. Meaning from other women.`,
  "4#ב": `And mole on forehead — Rambam holds mole: any with hair or large is not blemish even in woman — only specifically on face; Beit Yosef challenged from what is challenged here and here disqualified — should have challenged "he saw and was appeased"; appears to answer: challenger did not wish to challenge first "he saw and was appeased" — can answer in any blemish that is blemish even in kohanim we do not say he saw and was appeased for he said explicitly on condition you have no blemishes and behold she has blemish — must say he did not see precisely intending on her; if intended on other blemishes he would have said besides this blemish. After he resolved it discusses small mole which is not blemish in kohen — only in woman you say blemish — with this he challenges well he saw and was appeased: here language on condition no blemishes contradicts — we must say no complete blemishes disqualifying even in kohen — if so this blemish does not harm her even in woman even if stringent in woman for he saw and was appeased; automatically regarding always visible it seems even if said on condition no vows (should read blemishes) betrothed as above — correct per Rambam; Tur wrote mole with hair or large disqualifies even on whole body; Rambam's explanation more reasonable; Beit Yosef in name of Rashbatz: woman urinating in bed not among disqualifying blemishes in women — not mentioned in Gemara at all; and wonder bad odor and sweat — these are different being attached during relations, etc.; even for those who rule blemish — since grew with her sister he knew and was appeased, etc.; Beit Yosef disputes this is great blemish — simple. If so tanna of baraita should have said "they added in women," etc. in thought also (Maharach ztz"l should read: this mole was an addition) — it seems regarding ketubah certainly she did not lose; but to force dwell with her because of cherem Rabbenu Gershom practiced now — not included and can divorce against her will since dispute in laws mentioned here in Tur regarding blemishes found in woman and unknown when born — he wrote them in Shulchan Arukh below (siman 117).`,
  "7#_": `That there not be blemishes in her — emended in Tur; if so must distinguish between on condition no blemish on her or that there not be, etc.; even though Tosafot wrote and Beit Yosef brings no dependence of reason on language since he said no blemish on her and behold blemish on her — if so why say there if condition on him no blemishes and blemishes found if he healed betrothed — what difference him from her? Tosafot's intent law not dependent on mentioning blemishes; but language "that there not be" implies helps if healed; only difficult no source for this; in second version this matter absent — rather as written here in previous seif meaning condition on him — then healing helps; difference between them: husband particular about woman even if blemishes healed when he remembers her form when she had blemish; unlike woman not particular about this.`,
});

